From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christian Pfeiffer <cpfeiffer@rev-crew.info>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 02:43:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] Fix x86_64 Windows DHooks thiscall detours without params

Fixes alliedmodders/sourcemod#2282.

On x86_64 Windows, ConstructCallingConvention inserts the this pointer
of a thiscall as the first argument of the calling convention (in RCX),
but not into the setup's params. UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes then
indexed both by the convention's arguments: for a thiscall without
params, it wrote to an empty params vector, which crashed in
DynamicDetour.Enable, and for other thiscalls, every param got the size
of the register before it.

Skip the this pointer there, as alliedmodders/sourcemod#2290 did, which
was closed unmerged. Only x86_64 Windows inserts it, so the skip is
limited to that, as the insertion is.

Tested with Day of Infamy's 64-bit Windows server (srcds_x64): enabling
a post detour of CINSRules::ShouldBeWaitingForPlayers() const crashes
the server with master and works with this patch, both under Wine
(wine-cachyos 10.0) with DHooks built with clang-cl and xwin's MSVC
libraries, and on Windows 11 built with MSVC 14.52 (Visual Studio
2026). On Windows 11, detours of thiscalls with params crashed with
master as well, and work with this patch.

The params of thiscalls on x86_64 Windows still read wrong values after
this; the next patch, of register params' values on Windows, fixes
that and builds on this one.
---
 extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp b/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp
index dbb0abc7..970eeaa2 100644
--- a/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp
+++ b/extensions/dhooks/dynhooks_sourcepawn.cpp
@@ -309,7 +309,15 @@ bool UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes(CHook* pDetour, HookSetup *setup)
 	std::vector<DataTypeSized_t> &argTypes = callingConvention->m_vecArgTypes;
 	int numArgs = argTypes.size();
 
-	for (int i = 0; i < numArgs; i++)
+	// ConstructCallingConvention inserts the this pointer of a thiscall as the first argument on
+	// x86_64 Windows, which isn't one of the setup's params.
+	int firstArg = 0;
+#if defined(DYNAMICHOOKS_x86_64) && defined(WIN32)
+	if (setup->callConv == CallConv_THISCALL)
+		firstArg = 1;
+#endif
+
+	for (int i = firstArg; i < numArgs; i++)
 	{
 		// Ignore regular arguments on the stack.
 		if (argTypes[i].custom_register == None)
@@ -321,7 +329,7 @@ bool UpdateRegisterArgumentSizes(CHook* pDetour, HookSetup *setup)
 			return false;
 
 		argTypes[i].size = reg->m_iSize;
-		setup->params[i].size = reg->m_iSize;
+		setup->params[i - firstArg].size = reg->m_iSize;
 	}
 
 	return true;
